Workstream ID: blocker-card-status
Title: Show saved blocker status with red and green mission cards
Status: DONE
Milestone: Make persisted blocker status immediately visible
Dependencies: None
GitHub issue: https://github.com/Zanark/CareerOS/issues/28
Purpose: Make the mission's blocker editor red when a blocker is saved and
  green when none is saved. Use the validated workspace state, not unsaved
  textarea content. Preserve existing save/clear and failure behavior.
  Initially kept local for review; later publication is authorized and
  verified through local-refinements-publication.

Tasks:
  [x] Trace saved blocker, draft input and successful/failed commit behavior.
  [x] Add scoped red/green card treatment and non-color status information.
  [x] Qualify save/clear/reload, unsaved edits and rejected storage writes.
  [x] Check both themes, narrow layouts and existing blocker/mission guards.
  [x] Update focused documentation and prepare original tracking/continuity.
  [x] Prepare the preserved current-source preview for local review.

Acceptance criteria:
  The mission blocker card is red for a saved nonempty blocker and green when
    clear, using the same saved-state predicate as existing mission actions.
  Draft typing or deletion does not pretend a blocker was saved or cleared.
  A rejected save retains the previous status/color, data and visible error.
  Reloading and switching missions show the corresponding saved blocker state.
  Both themes retain readable fields/buttons and a visible status outline/tint.
  A flag/check and actual accessible text supplement the color.
  Planned missions remain disabled; no new eligibility or progress is inferred.
  Existing form labels, tutorial targets, save/clear rules and schemas remain.
  No owner browser/profile, backup import/reset or unauthorized publication.
  Technical verification remains separate from pending human review.

